    },
    {
      "figure_id": "Fig. 4",
      "caption": "Real-time measurements of <sup>fl</sup>uorescence intensity (A) and $\\mathrm { O D } _ { 6 0 0 }$ (B) of the mutants during the whole process of continuous evolution. The process was performed in two stages, in which the bestcharacterized mutant from the <sup>fi</sup>rst phase (0<sup>–</sup>380 h) was forced to the second phase of continuous evolution (381<sup>–</sup>550 h) for further evolution. The data points in (A) marked with open triangles or squares indicate that samples at those time points were selected for offline characterization. The data points in (B) labeled with arrows indicate the time points for introduction of 0.1% w/v L-arabinose for induction.",
      "related_paragraphs": [
        "2_3_improvement_of_galp_glk_dependent_e_coli_in_an_automatic_continuous_evolutionary_system_p003",
